This project has a graphify knowledge graph at graphify-out/.

- Graphify is one option among grep/file-search/read — not mandatory. Use it when it's the cheapest path to the answer (relational/impact/architecture questions), where `graphify query "<question>"` (or `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` / `graphify explain "<concept>"`) returns a small scoped subgraph instead of many full-file reads. For local/known-target lookups, grep/file-search is usually cheaper. See the "Code navigation" section in `project-context.mdc` (authoritative).
- If graphify-out/wiki/index.md exists, navigate it instead of reading raw files
- Read graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture review or when query/path/explain do not surface enough context
- After modifying code files in this session, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost)
